 "notes": "Beacon Rock, the southern tip of the Sha'ab Mahmud reef, with the south cardinal beacon on the reef top and the Dunraven upside down at the foot of the wall just south-west of it. Reef edge, beacon and the 2017 wreck from OpenStreetMap (the reef outline there is coarse); the wreck position from dive guides. Dives are dropped by zodiac and drift along the wall back to the boat; drop point and drift direction depend on the current and are approximate.",
